  "finalText": "Confirmed: the typecheck errors are pre-existing and identical before/after my change. The lint passes cleanly.\n\n**The fix** (`apps/extension/src/commands.ts:212-214`): Added a `finally` block to `runCli` that unconditionally calls `statusBar?.render(client)`.\n\n**Why this works:**\n\n- `statusBar?.indexing()` (line 192) sets \"indexing…\" at the start\n- `refreshAll()` calls `this.refresh()` which runs `client.reload()` → `provider.refresh()` → `statusBar.render()` in sequence — if either of the first two throws, `render()` is never reached and the status bar stays stuck on \"indexing…\"\n- The new `finally` block guarantees `statusBar.render(client)` runs after every path (success, `!result.ok`, exception), even if `refreshAll()` throws. It re-reads `client.status()` and `client.lastBuildError` to derive the correct final state:\n  - Index available → shows file/symbol counts\n  - Index unavailable + error set → shows \"build failed\" with the error tooltip\n  - Index unavailable + no error → shows \"no index\"",
